    "description": "Play through previously released games. All in the app and without internet connection!\r\n\r\nAlso, you can take a screenshot of the current Connections game and select it for use in Connections Archive Game app. When you do that, you can start dragging words into the grid and organize until you have the correct rows. Where the original game often has more than one word that might fit a row, you can drag the same word to multiple rows in this playground app. The purpose is to give you an alternative way to move words around on the Connections game board\r\n\r\nIf the word mistakenly doesn't upload from the screenshot, you can type in the word and add it to the words box.\r\n\r\nPress and Hold on a word to delete from the grid.\r\n\r\nWhen you're certain of your choices, you can go back to the actual  game and put in your choices.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Connections Game Archive is not affiliated with, nor has it been authorized, sponsored, or otherwise approved by The New York Times Company. You should definitely check out the NYT Connections game on New York Times website.",
